      "writtenOn": "2019-01-11T13:54:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "UIDs aren\u0027t changed by rematching, but that\u0027s not enough to say that updateNC can\u0027t have been called by rematchNetworkAndRequests. If an agent updates its UID, that will trigger a rematch, and if as a result a network changes foreground state, then you could come here having been called by rematchNetworkAndRequests. But I think now that in this case it\u0027s also not possible that the UIDs will have changed. So while what I was saying about this being reentered in the middle of itself is (I think) true, it was already the case. Your patch is simply doing the same thing as is already done for other things.\n\nAlso I think you\u0027re right, a VPN can\u0027t be a background network which prevents this from happening anyway.",
      "parentUuid": "af91be11_866622fd",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 5092,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 5093,
        "endChar": 84
      },
