      "writtenOn": "2019-01-10T18:54:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "My understanding is this: with added \"equalsUids\" check in updateCapabilities, it now goes into \"else\" branch, which causes two callbacks for this request:\n1) rematchAllNetworksAndRequests(nai, oldScore) is causing CALLBACK_AVAILABLE, which I believe also causes onCapabilitiesChanged.\n2) notifyNetworkCallbacks(nai, ConnectivityManager.CALLBACK_CAP_CHANGED) causes onCapabilitiesChanged explicitly.\n\nMy first thought wast to swap those two, but then I get the opposite problem - onCapabilitiesChanged is invoked before onLost when the app is removed from uids.\n\nSo it looks like to fix it I should change the code to only send CALLBACK_CAP_CHANGED to requests that were already satisfied by the network, and so didn\u0027t get CALLBACK_AVAILABLE.\n\nDoes this make sense? If so do you have any hints on what is the most elegant way to do it?",
      "parentUuid": "48ffae37_edb292f8",
